//// Decision 12 — an unnamed variant payload is refused, with a **located**
//// diagnostic that names the field form. A payload nobody can name is a
//// payload no `case` arm can bind, so `Circle(i32)` is not a shorter
//// `Circle(radius: i32)`; it is a declaration the language does not have.
////
//// Measured at `c748631e`, before C-08: the form reached the generic
//// `error: this token cannot appear here` with `unexpected `)`` — located at
//// the wrong token (the `)` after the type, not the payload), and naming
//// nothing. The row asked for a named diagnostic; this cell pins it.

type Shape { Circle(i32), Square(side: i32) }

pub fn main() {
    val s: Shape = Shape.Square(side: 2);
    @print("unreachable");
}
